flowchart LR
  accTitle: Secure Data Flow and Trust Boundaries
  accDescr: Coordinator and adviser browsers use the Flutter public client over trusted local HTTPS. Laravel authenticates roles, creates or opens authenticated envelopes through OpenSSL, reads an ignored server keyring, stores workflow and replay receipts in MariaDB, and writes allowlisted audit metadata. Rejected invalid, altered, expired, replayed, or unauthorized requests return safe errors without plaintext.
  coordinator["Coordinator browser"]
  adviser["Assigned adviser browser"]
  flutter["Flutter Web public client"]
  tls["Local TLS gateway TLS 1.2 or later"]
  auth["Laravel API Session authentication and role authorization"]
  exchange["SecureExchange service AES 256 GCM authenticated encryption"]
  keyring["Ignored protected keyring Server only"]
  database["MariaDB Workflow and unique replay receipts"]
  audit["Allowlisted audit records No tokens keys ciphertext or request bodies"]
  reject["Safe rejection Correlation reference and no plaintext"]
  coordinator -->|Fictional controlled input| flutter
  adviser -->|Envelope submission| flutter
  flutter -->|HTTPS JSON and bearer session| tls
  tls -->|Loopback forwarding after TLS termination| auth
  auth -->|Scoped workflow query| database
  auth -->|Minimized record or envelope| exchange
  exchange -->|Active or previous key by key ID| keyring
  exchange -->|One unique accepted message ID| database
  auth -->|Outcome and correlation only| audit
  exchange -.->|Tamper expiry invalid key or replay| reject
  auth -.->|Unauthenticated or unauthorized| reject
  exchange -->|Ciphertext on send or verified plaintext on receive| auth
  auth -->|No store response| tls
  tls -->|HTTPS response| flutter
